WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.860
- I've already taken cheeseburger,

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.610
and chicken burger, and French fries set,

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:06.835
and a bit of coke.

00:00:06.835 --> 00:00:09.502
(pensive music)

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.170
Double cheeseburger.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.373
Thanks, God, the same one, the same.

00:00:30.521 --> 00:00:33.354
(people cheering)

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.110
- This new chain is replacing McDonald's,

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.880
which is one of the
most high-profile brands

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:47.563
to leave Russian after the
Russian invasion of Ukraine.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.840
- [Sofiya] Here you can see the menu.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.910
Okay, breakfast.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.227
I think it's also the same.

00:00:58.659 --> 00:01:03.076
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:01:04.086 --> 00:01:08.586
(Stepan speaking in foreign language)

00:01:10.318 --> 00:01:14.651
(Oleg speaking in foreign language)

00:01:25.004 --> 00:01:28.208
- Opening of the first McDonald's in 1990

00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:29.841
was still when the Soviet Union

00:01:29.841 --> 00:01:32.121
was intact was very symbolic.

00:01:32.121 --> 00:01:34.960
It was seen as Russia's
opening to the West.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.940
People enjoyed McDonald's.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.360
There was something
that they could count on

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.940
on long road trips.

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:43.300
They knew what the quality is going to be.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.070
They knew it's going to be clean,

00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:46.720
the standards are there.

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:50.400
And they could count on
what they were going to eat.

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.000
- Every member in my family

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.790
has a favorite food set.

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.030
My mum loves Caesar roll,

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.530
my grandma likes potato wedges.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:05.032
And I can say that I'm really
big fan of the old McDonald's.

00:02:05.032 --> 00:02:07.699
(pensive music)

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:25.090
- Politicians in Russia

00:02:25.090 --> 00:02:26.620
are positioning this reopening

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:30.430
as a way to show that Russia can do well

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:35.170
despite all the sanctions and
the boycotts by corporations.

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.520
It's kind of an easy case

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:39.320
that won't prove much.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.110
Sure, they will be able to make burgers

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.140
but will they be able to make cars?

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:46.371
Will they be able to make airplanes?

00:02:46.371 --> 00:02:51.371
(pensive music)
(voices murmuring)

00:02:55.525 --> 00:02:57.503
(server speaking in foreign language)

00:02:57.503 --> 00:02:59.470
- What happens next is unclear.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.340
McDonald's hasn't commented on that.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:06.340
McDonald's can bid on the
franchise again in the future.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.510
We don't know whether it does so

00:03:08.510 --> 00:03:09.960
and under what circumstances.

